xpression after RNAi, using the honeybee knockdown/cuticle evidence of [(Costa et al., 2016-12)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/6825b2c91813dac9f2a92fe49b9d9515730311a1) and the crab cuticle-hardening evidence of [(Chung et al., 2012-09)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/1de3b7fa921646bff68bf0f5d3fff66127d30460) as baselines. Finally, treat the miRNA and CcTRPM/temperature components as exploratory: add target-site conservation, multiple prediction tools, negative controls, and CcTRPM knockdown/rescue or temperature time-course controls, because none of the related work directly supports miRNA targeting of Bursicon or low-temperature regulation of Bursicon in C. chinensis.",
