  "contradictions": "The strongest challenge is that the proposed method relies on reduced and non-reduced SDS-PAGE alone to demonstrate homodimer and heterodimer formation, but the closest precedent, [(An et al., 2012-03)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/d13d2385da6e3e694e90b6909bb4e7bf070c18c4), reported only qualitative non-reducing bands and did not provide quantitative band intensities, exact molecular weights, subunit-specific detection, or statistical significance, so SDS-PAGE alone may not unambiguously distinguish CcBurs-α/CcBurs-α, CcBurs-β/CcBurs-β, and CcBurs-α/CcBurs-β if the subunits have similar sizes. The next strongest limitation is that none of the cited studies used HEK293T co-expression; [(An et al., 2012-03)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/d13d2385da6e3e694e90b6909bb4e7bf070c18c4) used recombinant Drosophila subunits, [(Chung et al., 2012-09)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/1de3b7fa921646bff68bf0f5d3fff66127d30460) used recombinant crab CasBurs, and [(Zhang et al., 2017-02)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/eedba163fc5a0de6b3b4a6cb49abb5f870ba4736) used recombinant Aedes bursicon, so the assumption that HEK293T cells will produce correctly disulfide-bonded, secreted, and detectable CcBurs dimers is an extrapolation that may be affected by host-specific folding, glycosylation, secretion, and tag placement. A further contradiction to the sufficiency of the method is that [(Loy et al., 2007-08)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/588203316420b7498cd2fcff77e466689f9d95cc) provides only transcript-level evidence from honeybee larvae, with RT-PCR and sequencing of two ORFs, and no protein-level dimerization data, so it cannot support the structural claim that the CcBurs subunits form homodimers or heterodimers. Finally, [(Chung et al., 2012-09)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/1de3b7fa921646bff68bf0f5d3fff66127d30460) and [(Zhang et al., 2017-02)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/eedba163fc5a0de6b3b4a6cb49abb5f870ba4736) provide functional evidence for heterodimeric or homodimeric Bursicon activity but do not report reduced/non-reduced SDS-PAGE dimer quantification, so they do not validate the proposed structural assay.",
